30,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"I watched the mornings. Four times, someone had to move a bike to get theirs out. The row under the eaves is the only dry spot.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The ledger shows no capital reserve. Adding a billing system means a new levy. I need to know if households can absorb that.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,The minutes confirm my fear. The same flats held the covered spots for five years. No one ever voted to change it.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The complaints were all about bikes leaning on each other. No one asked for a fix. The ward park has a waitlist.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The frame trial was rough. Greasing it twice a year is a chore. If we buy it, someone has to remember to do it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@George, if the covered spots were never voted on, we can reset them. The rain data proves the eaves are the only logical priority.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, resetting them is free, but adding a management system is not. The treasurer’s file shows the admin time is already high.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,The neighboring block tried charging. Two households stopped paying and stopped attending meetings. It fractured their community.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,The ward park is full. We can’t just tell people to go there. We have to solve this internally without breaking the peace.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"If we choose the frame, the greasing is the killer. It’s not just money, it’s the recurring physical effort that no one wants.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The bottleneck is the eaves. If we assign those by rotation, the morning shoving stops. It’s a simple logical fix.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Rotation is free. But if we add a sticker system to track it, we add cost. I am leaning toward the free option.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"The neighbor’s failure was about money, not fairness. A simple rotation avoids the financial friction that caused their conflict.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,The complaints died because no one owned the problem. A rotation rule is passive. It doesn’t require a manager to enforce it.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"Passive is good. If the rule is just ""first come, first served"" for the eaves, there is no greasing, no billing, no work.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I propose a strict rotation for the dry spots. No money, no frames. Just a schedule. It solves the rain and the shoving.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. The financial risk is zero. The administrative risk is low. It is the only option that doesn’t drain the account.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"It is fair. It removes the historical bias I found in the minutes. It treats every resident equally, regardless of who lived here first.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,It keeps the lobby quiet. No one has to argue about who owns a spot. It preserves the nodding we do in the hallway.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,And it means no one has to grease a spring or chase a bill. It is the only option that doesn’t create a new job for one person.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
