60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is out. The ledger shows no reserve for the admin work. It creates a financial burden we cannot sustain.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,I concur. Option A requires a billing system. The treasurer’s file shows the current admin load is already at capacity.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,Option A is the neighbor’s mistake. It turns a shared resource into a commodity. It invites the resentment I saw in the minutes.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A creates a class of ""owners"" and ""renters."" That is exactly the kind of division that turns neighbors into rivals.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option A means someone has to chase the non-payers. That is a job. I do not want to be the one with the phone.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is chaotic. The morning departures show that without assigned spots, the shoving match continues. It fails to solve the rain issue.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is free, but it fails the usage test. The rain exposure data shows that without priority, the dry spots are contested daily.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"Option B is fair in theory, but in practice, it rewards the early riser. It does not address the historical bias of who gets the best spot.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B is a free-for-all. The complaints log shows that when no one owns the space, everyone blames the space. It creates friction.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"Option B means no one is responsible for the racks. If a rack breaks, no one fixes it. It is a passive failure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Option C is the logical choice. It is free, it is fair, and it removes the morning shoving. The rotation is the key.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Option C has zero financial cost. It requires no new admin. It is the only option that aligns with the building’s current financial reality.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"Option C is the only one that treats all residents equally. It removes the historical bias. It is a clean, fair reset.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is passive. It does not require a manager. It does not create a new job. It preserves the social peace of the lobby.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"Option C is the only one that doesn’t create a recurring physical task. No greasing, no billing, no chasing. It is sustainable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I vote for C. It solves the rain, the shoving, and the fairness. It is the only logical solution.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for C. The financial risk is zero. The administrative risk is minimal. It is the responsible choice.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I vote for C. It is fair. It is equal. It removes the bias. It is the right thing to do.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for C. It keeps the peace. It avoids the conflict. It is the calm choice.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,I vote for C. It is the only one that doesn’t leave me with a wrench. It is the sustainable choice.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
